anggraph_factory/graph.py:build_curriculum_factory_graph`) — see\n\"P-N31-001 correction\" below.\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls the D16-D23 function\nbodies directly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged\nstep-to-step through the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), and\nseparately exercises the real compiled graph end to end for the wiring proof.\n\n## P-N31-001 correction: D16-D23 wired into the one production compiled graph\n\nN90's audit (finding F1) found D16-D23 fully implemented and function-level\ntested but never registered into `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` — a real\nrun could never reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED`. Root cause: this\nnode's own `repair.py` docstring deferred registration to N32, whose prompt\ndeferred it right back. `graph.py` was added to this node's write set to\nclose the gap directly, without touching `unit_graph.py` (N30's frozen,\ncorrect table) or `workbook.py`/D24-D32 (N32's write).\n\nWhat changed in `graph.py`:\n\n- `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` — `binding_inventory()` plus\n  `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` (D16-D23). `binding_inventory()`\n  itself is untouched, byte-for-byte, so `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`'s own\n  tests that recompute their expectation directly from its return value stay\n  correct (verified directly, see TEST evidence below).\n- `full_binding_inventory()` — `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` plus\n  `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`, for `register_workbook_topology`'s own\n  destination resolution (N32's concern; unchanged here beyond the rename of\n  its base call).\n- `register_unit_repair_topology(builder, available)` — a thin, additive\n  wrapper around `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path`, called once from\n  `build_curriculum_factory_graph` immediately after `register_skeleton`,\n  wiring the loop *internal* to D16-D23 (D17→D18→D19→[deterministic producer\n  or D90→M06]→D20→D21→earliest invalidated producer/check→D16; D16 PASS→\n  D22→D23→D05; D17/D18 bound-exhausted→D98). The six `unit_graph.\n  DEFERRED_EDGES` rows N31 owns (D08/D09/D12/D14/D91→D17, M05→D16) are *not*\n  added by this function — they are `unit_graph.py`'s own rows and resolve\n  automatically the moment D16/D17 are members of the bindings\n  `register_skeleton` receives, exactly as `unit_graph.register_unit_path`\n  was already designed to do.\n- `build_curriculum_factory_graph` now compiles against\n  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` instead of `binding_inventory()`, and\n  calls `register_unit_repair_topology` right after `register_skeleton`.\n\n`unit_graph.py`, `workbook.py`, and D24-D32 are untouched by this node.\n\n### Required proof (P-N31-001), executed against the real compiled graph\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` (from\n`test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`\nonward):\n\n- D16-D23 and M06 are members of `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...).\n  get_graph().nodes` (a real compiled graph, `compiled.get_graph().nodes` —\n  not a declared table).\n- Each of the six `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows owned by\n  `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` is a real edge in `compiled_topology(compiled)`\n  (evidence: `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_\n  topology.txt`, all six rows `wired=True`).\n- `binding_inventory()`'s return value is unchanged (asserted disjoint from\n  `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` and structurally identical to its\n  pre-wiring definition).\n- `validate_bindings`/`register_unit_path` raise no `GraphBindingError`/\n  `UnitTopologyError` against the widened bindings.\n- A real run through the compiled production graph (fake-CLI-transport,\n  scripted-response pattern from `test_plan26_adversarial.py`) reaches\n  `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for a real unit twice: once via the D16\n  PASS fast path\n  (`test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`)\n  and once via a full D17-D21 repair-and-retest loop back to D16 for a\n  deterministic-repair-owned finding\n  (`test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`).\n\n## Owner / retest map\n\n| Owner | Channel | Repair route | First retest node |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |\n| curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |\n| unit content | content | model (M06) | `D09_VALIDATE_CONTENT` |\n| unit visual | visuals | model (M06) unless every named key is an authoritative/library brief, then deterministic | `D10_COMPILE_VISUAL_BRIEFS` |\n| unit layout | layout | deterministic (boundary-scoped pointer correction) | `D13_RENDER_UNIT` |\n\n`repair.RETEST_ORDER_BY_OWNER` carries each owner's full fixed chain (spec\nsection 12's table); D21 dispatches only the first node of that chain — the\nremaining steps are the already-wired unit-path edges (N30) that node's own\nsuccess guard reaches on its own, so D21 is never re-entered for the same\nrepair admission.\n\nFrozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17\nowns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns\nthe numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`).\n\n## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)\n\nRecomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before\nminting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.\nCategories enforced: source admission (sha256-resolved), domain check set\n(`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content check set\n(`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join result,\npage inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one\nindependent unit review with every blocking finding's `category` mapped\nthrough the code-owned `owner_for_review_category()` table (never trusted\nverbatim from the model), and repair-request closure (no request left\nunresolved). `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject`\nindependently removes/fails each of the five owner-bearing categories and\nconfirms D22 raises every time; `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`\nconfirms a check recorded against a superseded head is invisible to the\nreduction (stale evidence cannot pass) — `compute_unit_denominator` only\ncounts a check whose `head_hash` equals the *current* head.\n\nDocumented scope limit, unchanged from generation 1: this denominator treats\nthe append-only evidence/log layer and the LangGraph checkpoint layer as\nstructurally present (state reducers already enforce their shape) rather\nthan independently re-auditing their hash chain from inside D22 (spec\nsection 13.1 items 13-14). `acceptance.py`'s module docstring records this.\n\n## Real-D98 traces (TEST 9)\n\n`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` imports\n`runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal` unmodified and calls\n`terminal.write_terminal()` directly — the identical function N22 wrote,\nnever a stand-in:\n\n- `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`:\n  a `UNIT_ACCEPTED` candidate built from real D22/D23 output is\n  independently re-derived and accepted by D98's own `_validate_unit_accepted`.\n- `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`: the\n  same candidate with a forged `receipt_hash` is rejected and D98 writes\n  `SYSTEM_FAILURE` in its place — no N31 code decided that; D98's own\n  re-derivation did.\n- `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`:\n  the `terminal_candidate` D18 proposes on attempt-bound exhaustion is\n  independently accepted by D98's `_validate_exhausted`.\n\nNo test in this file, and no code in `repair.py`/`acceptance.py`, writes to\n`nodes/terminal.py`; `terminal.write_terminal.__module__` is asserted to\nstill be `runtime.langgraph_factory.nodes.terminal`.\n\n## P-N31-003 correction: two residual `test_plan26_unit_graph.py` failures closed\n\nOnce D16-D23 were wired (P-N31-001), two tests in `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`\n(not this node's write set at the time) failed because their premises had\nbeen inverted by the wiring itself. P-N31-003 added that one file to this\nnode's write set, scoped to exactly these two tests:\n\n1. `test_the_unobservable_boundary_is_excluded_for_a_stated_reason` — its own\n   docstring pre-assigned N31 as the owner of the rewrite once D16-D23 are\n   wired. Before wiring, M05's update never reached the stream because the\n   branch that would emit it resolved to the then-deferred\n   `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_EVIDENCE` and aborted the superstep. `D16_REDUCE_UNIT_\n   EVIDENCE` is now a real node body, so M05's update is genuinely\n   observable; the test now asserts that inversion directly instead of the\n   retired exclusion. `REACHABLE_BOUNDARIES`/`UNOBSERVABLE_BOUNDARY` and\n   every other test that depends on them are untouched.\n2. `test_a_fresh_episode_executes_the_bootstrap_spine_once_through_langgraph`\n   — a real, reproducible LangGraph `stream(stream_mode=\"updates\")` artifact:\n   the chunk for a step whose *next* step's routing raises in the same tick\n   is never yielded, so the clean one-unit episode's second\n   `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` call (which correctly finds the manifest exhausted\n   and routes to the still-deferred `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`,\n   raising `KeyError` in the same tick) is undercounted by exactly one in\n   `result[\"trace\"]`. The real, checkpointed final state is unaffected by\n   this streaming artifact. The test now asserts the checkpointed state\n   directly (`state[\"selected_unit_id\"] is None`,\n   `state[\"cursor\"][\"accepted_ordinal\"] == 1`) instead of inferring the\n   outcome from a trace count this specific stream/exception interaction\n   cannot reliably produce. `compiled.stream()`'s call, mode, and\n   `graph.py`/`unit_graph.py` are untouched.\n\n## Commands and results\n\n```\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py\n=> 38 passed\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n\n/tmp/plan26_n30_verify/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py\n=> 93 passed\n(results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/focused_test_run.txt)\n```\n\nBoth required verification commands are fully green: 93/93 for\n`test_plan26_unit_graph.py` (including both P-N31-003 corrections), and\n38/38 for `test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` (32 generation-1 tests plus 6\nP-N31-001 required-proof tests).\n\n`results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/full_plan26_suite.txt` (full\n`-k plan26` run, not a required verification command) shows one unrelated\nfailure, `test_plan26_prompt_graph_controller.py::\ntest_passed_nodes_remain_admissible_after_harness_or_predecessor_change`,\nasserting `N20_GRAPH_COMPILER` is admissible off the live receipt store.\nNeither `repair.py`, `acceptance.py`, `graph.py`, nor either test file this\nnode writes touches `prompt_graph_controller.py` or any receipt file, and\nnone of them are in this node's declared writable-paths set.\n\n## Hashes\n\n| File | SHA-256 (shasum -a 256) |\n|---|---|\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` | `976b47410a001b58b9b5c8be62b2bda21ea2fce0feed5744a953d0ae4b05bb23` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` | `9752736b326e0d58c42affd2166177c42cc0db74626e2b4d83783c8024be1bed` |\n| `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py` | `efabbd515c4ba2aab811e47a88ac2ffe2742a23fec9b7e46060ec7e385f06aaa` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` | `de6552e7f6d419405ae2cceb619087cc07bf358cc72a6a006cb17b2e3c769385` |\n| `tests/runtime/test_plan26_unit_graph.py` | `db62b49c511cea3cc72e6427fdda0fb356f22e5be5dcb00cc6c3a91f4885e54d` |\n\n## TEST item verdicts\n\n1. **PASSED** — `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_no_owner`,\n   `test_d17_rejects_a_finding_with_an_unknown_owner`,\n   `test_d17_partitions_a_multi_owner_findings_list_into_separate_owner_entries`,\n   `test_review_finding_category_is_never_trusted_as_an_owner`.\n2. **PASSED** — `test_a_correctly_scoped_model_repair_admits`,\n   `test_a_broad_repair_outside_its_boundary_is_refused`,\n   `test_an_in_place_no_op_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_stale_parent_repair_is_refused`,\n   `test_a_deterministic_layout_repair_changes_only_its_allowed_pointer`.\n3. **PASSED** — `test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child`,\n   `test_fingerprint_repeat_bound_exhausts_at_d17`.\n4. **PASSED** — `test_d21_dispatches_the_first_retest_node_of_the_owners_fixed_chain`,\n   `test_stale_evidence_at_an_old_head_cannot_pass_the_denominator`.\n5. **PASSED** — `test_d22_accepts_a_fully_passing_denominator`,\n   `test_removing_or_failing_any_single_member_makes_d22_reject` (×5),\n   `test_staling_the_content_head_makes_d22_reject`.\n6. **PASSED** — `test_accept_once_refuses_a_differing_second_write_for_the_same_unit`,\n   `test_an_already_accepted_unit_can_never_re_enter_classification_or_planning`.\n7. **PASSED** — `test_d23_writes_checkpoint_metadata_and_cursor_in_the_same_update`,\n   `test_d23_refuses_to_advance_the_cursor_with_no_accepted_receipt`.\n8. **PASSED** — `test_coverage_proof_rejects_missing_extra_reordered_and_wrong_hash`.\n9. **PASSED** — `test_a_unit_accepted_candidate_traverses_the_real_d98_and_is_accepted`,\n   `test_a_tampered_unit_accepted_candidate_is_rejected_by_the_real_d98`,\n   `test_a_convergence_exhausted_candidate_from_d17_traverses_the_real_d98`.\n10. **PASSED** — `test_repeating_d22_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_repeating_d23_after_a_crash_replays_idempotently`,\n    `test_re_admitting_the_same_repair_after_the_head_already_advanced_fails_closed`,\n    `test_a_crash_before_the_terminal_write_still_lets_d98_be_invoked_cleanly`.\n\nP-N31-001 required proof (compiled-graph wiring): **PASSED** —\n`test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`,\n`test_binding_inventory_return_value_is_unchanged_by_this_nodes_wiring`,\n`test_the_six_n31_owned_deferred_edges_are_now_real_wired_edges`,\n`test_widening_the_bindings_raises_no_topology_or_binding_error`,\n`test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`,\n`test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`.\n\n## Known scope limitations (for N32 and future generations)\n\n- The deterministic-vs-model routing table for `source interpretation` is\n  simplified to always route to M06; spec section 12 allows a deterministic\n  refetch when a locator remains authorized, which would require a\n  source-retrieval integration outside this node's write set\n  (`repair.py`'s module docstring records the reasoning).\n- `compute_unit_denominator()`'s coverage of spec section 13.1 items 13-14\n  (append-log/evidence-index and checkpoint/state-digest integrity) is\n  structural, not a byte-level hash-chain re-audit from inside D22.\n- D24-D32 (N32's workbook engine) remain absent from\n  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()`/the production compile point, exactly as\n  `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` still documents for `D05_SELECT_NEXT_UNIT` →\n  `D24_PROVE_EXACT_MANIFEST_COVERAGE`; `workbook.py`, `unit_graph.py`, and\n  D24-D32 are untouched by this node.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":3,"oldLines":11,"newStart":3,"newLines":12,"lines":[" status: PASSED"," node_prompt: plans/26_langgraph_curriculum_factory/prompts/N31_repair_acceptance.prompt.v2.md"," predecessor: N30_UNIT_GRAPH (compact state supplied by the controller, status PASSED)","-generation: 1","+generation: 3","+patch_ids: [\"P-N31-001\", \"P-N31-002\", \"P-N31-003\"]"," "," ## What this node built"," ","-Two new top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns","+Two top-level modules, per `contracts/node_ownership.v1.md` (\"N31 owns"," repair/acceptance modules, not terminal.py\"):"," "," - `runtime/langgraph_factory/repair.py` — D17 (finding classification), D18"]},{"oldStart":15,"oldLines":34,"newStart":16,"newLines":87,"lines":["   (boundary-checked admission), D21 (retest dispatch)."," - `runtime/langgraph_factory/acceptance.py` — D16 (unit denominator","   reduction), D22 (recompute-and-accept), D23 (checkpoint correlation +","-  cursor advance), plus `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()`, the D24 coverage","-  predicate N32 will call.","+  cursor advance), `prove_exact_manifest_coverage()` (the D24 coverage","+  predicate N32 calls), `UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES`, and","+  `register_unit_repair_path()` (D16-D23's own internal edges)."," ","-Neither module is registered into the compiled graph yet. `routing.py`'s","-guard tables for D16-D23 already exist (built by N20) and this generation's","-functions emit exactly the guard values those tables declare","-(`unit_denominator_passed`/`unit_findings_repairable`,","-`partition_complete`/`convergence_exhausted`, `repair_planned`,","-`model_repair`/`deterministic_repair`, `repair_admitted`,","-`retest_frontier_incomplete`/`retest_frontier_complete`, `unit_accepted`,","-`checkpoint_correlated`) — but `add_node`/`add_conditional_edges` wiring","-these into `graph.py`'s `StateGraph` is N32's write","-(`implementation.graph.v3.yaml`: N32 owns `runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py`,","-N31 does not). Every function here is therefore a plain, narrowly-scoped","-`(state, runtime_context) -> update` callable in the same shape N23's","-`model_nodes.py` already uses for D90/D91 — not wrapped in","-`nodes.deterministic_node()`, since that decorator requires a","-`NODE_CATALOGUE` row this generation is not permitted to add (`nodes/__init__.py`","-is not in N31's write set). A future node binds these to catalogue rows","-without changing this module's bodies.","+D16-D23 are now real, wired members of the one compiled production graph","+(`runtime/langgraph_factory/graph.py:build_curriculum_factory_graph`) — see","+\"P-N31-001 correction\" below."," ","-`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls every function","-directly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged step-to-step","-through the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), not a mock merge.","+`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` calls the D16-D23 function","+bodies directly against hand-built `FactoryState` fixtures, merged","+step-to-step through the real field reducers (`state.FIELD_REDUCERS`), and","+separately exercises the real compiled graph end to end for the wiring proof."," ","+## P-N31-001 correction: D16-D23 wired into the one production compiled graph","+","+N90's audit (finding F1) found D16-D23 fully implemented and function-level","+tested but never registered into `build_curriculum_factory_graph()` — a real","+run could never reach `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED`. Root cause: this","+node's own `repair.py` docstring deferred registration to N32, whose prompt","+deferred it right back. `graph.py` was added to this node's write set to","+close the gap directly, without touching `unit_graph.py` (N30's frozen,","+correct table) or `workbook.py`/D24-D32 (N32's write).","+","+What changed in `graph.py`:","+","+- `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` — `binding_inventory()` plus","+  `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` (D16-D23). `binding_inventory()`","+  itself is untouched, byte-for-byte, so `test_plan26_unit_graph.py`'s own","+  tests that recompute their expectation directly from its return value stay","+  correct (verified directly, see TEST evidence below).","+- `full_binding_inventory()` — `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` plus","+  `workbook.WORKBOOK_NODE_BODIES`, for `register_workbook_topology`'s own","+  destination resolution (N32's concern; unchanged here beyond the rename of","+  its base call).","+- `register_unit_repair_topology(builder, available)` — a thin, additive","+  wrapper around `acceptance.register_unit_repair_path`, called once from","+  `build_curriculum_factory_graph` immediately after `register_skeleton`,","+  wiring the loop *internal* to D16-D23 (D17→D18→D19→[deterministic producer","+  or D90→M06]→D20→D21→earliest invalidated producer/check→D16; D16 PASS→","+  D22→D23→D05; D17/D18 bound-exhausted→D98). The six `unit_graph.","+  DEFERRED_EDGES` rows N31 owns (D08/D09/D12/D14/D91→D17, M05→D16) are *not*","+  added by this function — they are `unit_graph.py`'s own rows and resolve","+  automatically the moment D16/D17 are members of the bindings","+  `register_skeleton` receives, exactly as `unit_graph.register_unit_path`","+  was already designed to do.","+- `build_curriculum_factory_graph` now compiles against","+  `unit_repair_binding_inventory()` instead of `binding_inventory()`, and","+  calls `register_unit_repair_topology` right after `register_skeleton`.","+","+`unit_graph.py`, `workbook.py`, and D24-D32 are untouched by this node.","+","+### Required proof (P-N31-001), executed against the real compiled graph","+","+`tests/runtime/test_plan26_repair_acceptance.py` (from","+`test_d16_through_d23_and_m06_are_members_of_the_compiled_production_graph`","+onward):","+","+- D16-D23 and M06 are members of `build_curriculum_factory_graph(...).","+  get_graph().nodes` (a real compiled graph, `compiled.get_graph().nodes` —","+  not a declared table).","+- Each of the six `unit_graph.DEFERRED_EDGES` rows owned by","+  `N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE` is a real edge in `compiled_topology(compiled)`","+  (evidence: `results/evidence/N31_REPAIR_ACCEPTANCE/compiled_graph_","+  topology.txt`, all six rows `wired=True`).","+- `binding_inventory()`'s return value is unchanged (asserted disjoint from","+  `acceptance.UNIT_REPAIR_NODE_BODIES` and structurally identical to its","+  pre-wiring definition).","+- `validate_bindings`/`register_unit_path` raise no `GraphBindingError`/","+  `UnitTopologyError` against the widened bindings.","+- A real run through the compiled production graph (fake-CLI-transport,","+  scripted-response pattern from `test_plan26_adversarial.py`) reaches","+  `D22_ACCEPT_UNIT`/`UNIT_ACCEPTED` for a real unit twice: once via the D16","+  PASS fast path","+  (`test_a_clean_one_unit_episode_reaches_d22_accept_unit_via_the_d16_pass_fast_path`)","+  and once via a full D17-D21 repair-and-retest loop back to D16 for a","+  deterministic-repair-owned finding","+  (`test_a_full_d17_through_d21_repair_and_retest_loop_reaches_d22_accept_unit`).","+"," ## Owner / retest map"," ","-| Owner | Channel | Repair route (this generation) | First retest node |","+| Owner | Channel | Repair route | First retest node |"," |---|---|---|---|"," | source interpretation | domain | model (M06) | `D07_CORRELATE_AND_ADMIT_SOURCES` |"," | curriculum domain | domain | model (M06) | `D08_VALIDATE_DOMAIN` |"]},{"oldStart":58,"oldLines":21,"newStart":112,"newLines":16,"lines":[" "," Frozen limits, enforced exactly where spec section 6.2 assigns them: D17"," owns the repeated-fingerprint bound (`MAX_FINGERPRINT_REPEATS = 2`); D18 owns","-the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`). An earlier","-draft of this generation checked both bounds in D17, which made","-`test_attempt_bound_exhausts_before_a_fourth_repair_child` fail (D17 was","-exhausting a case the prompt's own TEST item expects D18 to exhaust) — fixed","-by removing the attempt-bound check from D17, per spec's own row split (\"D17","-... repeated bound = exhaustion\" vs. \"D18 ... attempt bound = exhaustion\").","+the numeric attempt bound (`MAX_REPAIR_CHILDREN_PER_CHAIN = 3`)."," "," ## Denominator trace (D16 / D22, `acceptance.compute_unit_denominator`)"," "," Recomputed identically by D16 (before repair) and D22 (immediately before"," minting an accepted receipt) off whatever heads are *current* at call time.","-Categories enforced this generation: source admission (sha256-resolved),","-domain check set (`DOMAIN_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), content","-check set (`CONTENT_CHECK_IDS`, matched by current head hash), visual join","-result, page inventory + inspection set (exact page count, all PASS), one","+